# Secrets: bot tokens and channel ids.
.env

# NOTE: .gitignore has no trailing comments. A line like
#     data/live/    # camera cache
# is treated as a literal pattern including the spaces and hash, matches
# nothing, and silently commits the thing you meant to exclude. Comments go on
# their own line, always.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER COMMIT: human subjects data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Usability sessions record verbatim quotes and observation notes. Participants
# are told their notes stay with us, and pseudonymous labels ("P3") do not make
# free-text quotes safe to publish. Keep these local, always.
data/user_tests.jsonl

# Unparsed chat messages. Raw text of what people typed, which routinely
# contains where they live and work ("Park Circus to my office"). The hashed
# user id keeps it pseudonymous, but the messages themselves do not belong in
# git. Read it locally with scripts/chat_misses.py.
data/chat_misses.jsonl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-fetched or regenerated on demand
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YOLO weights, auto-downloaded on first use.
*.pt

# Sample clips (~44 MB), downloaded by the vision scripts.
data/video/

# Camera stills and clip cache (~24 MB), rebuilt continuously at runtime.
data/live/

# Re-fetched from the TfL API and cached for a day.
data/livecam_registry.json

# Personas drift as feedback accumulates; reset_demo.py reseeds them.
data/profiles.json
# ...and any backup of it. These hold real Telegram user ids and the
# home/work addresses those people saved; none of that belongs in git.
data/profiles*.json

# A single stale computer-vision reading.
data/cv_observation.json

# Logs.
*.log
data/*.err

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately COMMITTED, for anyone wondering
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/live_observations.jsonl - the real collected traffic measurements. It is
#   the evidence base for every accuracy claim, and it cannot be regenerated
#   retroactively: it was gathered in wall-clock time. Contains only TfL camera
#   ids and vehicle counts from a public open-data feed, so nothing personal.
#   Committing it is also the only backup.
# data/city_*.json - imported road graphs. Regenerable, but the import takes
#   minutes and depends on a public API being up, so a clone that works offline
#   is worth the megabytes.
# data/validation.json, data/benchmark.json - published results the dashboard
#   reads and the README quotes.

# Generated by coverage runs and SonarQube scans; rebuilt on every scan.
.coverage
coverage.xml
.scannerwork/
.DS_Store
.DS_Store
